  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Keep only the degrees that can matter",
      "body": "<p>Multiplication by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> means that only the constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> coefficients inside the square brackets can contribute to the final <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> term.</p>",
      "recap": "Higher-degree terms can be ignored.",
      "pitfall": "Do not expand all powers when the target degree is small.",
      "pause": "Find the constant coefficient of the difference first.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l11",
          "reminder": "Targeted coefficient extraction tracks only degrees that can reach the requested power."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Find the inner quadratic coefficient",
      "body": "In the first inner power, a quadratic term can come from a single quadratic selection or from two linear selections. Count the bracket placements and numerical factors for both cases.",
      "recap": "Every selection with the target total degree contributes to its coefficient.",
      "pitfall": "Also check which low degrees can occur in the other inner power before taking their difference.",
      "pause": "Compute the inner constant and quadratic coefficients, then combine the outer and inner terms whose degrees sum to two.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l11",
          "reminder": "Every selection with the target total degree contributes to its coefficient."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> coefficient in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>78</mn></mrow></math>. The expression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> has constant term 1 and no x or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> terms.</p><p>The bracketed difference therefore has constant coefficient 0 and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> coefficient 78. Multiplication by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> coefficient <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>312</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer G: 312.</strong></p>",
